**assistant**:
> She is called “Professor” because LSE has formally appointed her **Professor in Practice of Natural Capital, Risk and Finance** at its Grantham Research Institute.
> 
> “Professor in Practice” is an academic professorial title typically awarded for exceptional real-world leadership and expertise, rather than requiring a conventional career as a tenure-track university professor. Ranger’s doctorate, research record, and extensive senior work across government, the World Bank, finance, climate policy, and sustainable-finance institutions support that appointment.
